Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Fri Sep 18 08:02:34 2026 -0500

    fix(api): return RFC3339 timestamps from the queue endpoints (OB-GAP-068)
    
    entryToWire copied the queue columns to the wire verbatim, so
    started_at/completed_at reached clients in SQLite's TEXT layout
    ("2026-08-15 02:13:43") and time.Parse(time.RFC3339, ...) / new Date(...)
    rejected every complete and failed entry, even though
    docs/api-reference.md and pkg/api/openapi.yaml QueueEntry promise RFC
    3339. Both fields also carried omitempty, so a pending entry dropped the
    keys entirely instead of returning "" the way the documented example
    shows.
    
    - formatStoreTimestamp: "" stays "", an already-RFC3339 value passes
      through unchanged, the store layout "2006-01-02 15:04:05" is parsed as
      UTC and re-formatted with time.RFC3339, and an unrecognised value is
      returned unchanged rather than guessed at or dropped.
    - entryToWire routes both fields through it, so one fix covers the list
      handler and the single-status handler (both call queueWireEntry).
    - drop omitempty from started_at/completed_at; failure_reason keeps its
      deliberate omitempty (DF-OFF-BY-ONE-4).
    - drop the stale comment pointing at parseSQLiteTimestamp, which does
      not exist in this repo, and document the conversion on ingest.Entry.
    - TestQueueTimestamps_RFC3339 + TestFormatStoreTimestamp in
      internal/api/handlers_test.go assert on the RAW response body, so a tag
      typo or a dropped key cannot pass behind the decoder.
    - docs: state the started_at/completed_at rule in api-reference.md and
      give both properties a description in the OpenAPI spec.
    
    Live proof on a scratch instance built from this change, against a
    .backup copy of the store: 3863 entries / 7726 timestamps, 0 RFC3339
    violations, no raw store layout survives to the wire, and a pending
    entry returns both keys as "". Against the pre-fix code the new
    regression test fails with the raw space format and the missing pending
    keys.
    
    Addresses OB-GAP-068.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
